& [LargeLanguageModelWalker] is the bounded project subject
  + [project_uuid] is 9a78e0ed-1223-49d1-b152-e1ff6ba72386
  + [display_name] is Large Language Model-Walker
  + [filesystem_name] is LargeLanguageModelWalker
  + [purpose] is coordinate intended meaning through composed and decomposed semantic anchors
  + [primary_surface] is a durable database of terms, contextual anchors, SOP references, file references, and turn intentions
  + [authority_state] is canonical_foundation

  - never: infer one universal meaning for a term when contextual anchors distinguish intended uses
  - never: allow an index record to replace the referenced source file as source authority
  - never: treat archived model inference as hidden-state inspection
  - never: let probabilistic model output silently become database, SOP, filesystem, Git, or specification authority

& [SemanticAnchor] is an identity-bearing point of intended meaning
  + [anchor_uuid] is the stable primary identity
  + [label] is the human-readable anchor name
  + [subject_scope] is the bounded subject in which the anchor has meaning
  + [intended_meaning] is the meaning the anchor coordinates
  + [anchor_kind] is term, context, intention, constraint, relation, source, file, SOP subject, or turn
  + [status] is proposed, active, superseded, disputed, or retired
  + [created_turn_uuid] is the originating turn record
  + [source_reference_set] is zero or more inspectable provenance references

& [TermRecord] is a durable term identity distinct from any one contextual meaning
  + [term_uuid] is the stable primary identity
  + [surface_form] is the written term
  + [normalized_form] is the comparison form
  + [anchor_set] is one or more SemanticAnchor references
  + [contextual_use_set] is the admissible intended-use records
  - never: collapse distinct contextual uses solely because their surface forms match

& [ContextualAnchor] is a SemanticAnchor specialized by context
  + [context_anchor_uuid] is the stable primary identity
  + [term_uuid] is the referenced TermRecord
  + [context_subject_uuid] is the bounded subject providing local meaning
  + [intended_use] is the purpose of the term in that subject
  + [qualifier_set] is roles, constraints, conditions, modality, audience, phase, or domain
  + [relation_set] is explicit edges to other anchors
  + [evidence_set] is source-derived support
  + [uncertainty] is unresolved meaning that must not be silently promoted

& [AnchorRelation] is a typed directed relation between semantic anchors
  + [relation_uuid] is the stable primary identity
  + [source_anchor_uuid] is the origin
  + [predicate] is composes_with, decomposes_to, references, specializes, contrasts_with, supersedes, supports, constrains, or intends
  + [target_anchor_uuid] is the destination
  + [composition_order] is optional ordering within a composition
  + [source_turn_uuid] is the turn that asserted the relation
  + [justification_reference] is the inspectable reason for the relation

& [CorrelationWeight] is a contextual scoring contribution between an input term or intention and an indexed semantic anchor
  + [weight_uuid] is the stable primary identity
  + [input_anchor_uuid] is the term, phrase, or intention anchor being evaluated
  + [candidate_anchor_uuid] is the indexed anchor receiving the contribution
  + [context_subject_uuid] is the bounded context in which the weight applies
  + [weight_kind] is lexical, contextual, relational, purpose, provenance, recency, authority, or negative_constraint
  + [weight_value] is a normalized numeric contribution with declared range and direction
  + [evidence_reference_set] is the inspectable basis for the weight
  + [weight_model_version] is the scoring-contract identity
  + [validity_state] is active, provisional, stale, disputed, or retired
  = must: keep contextual weights distinct from universal semantic truth
  = must: expose the component weights contributing to a ranked result

& [ResonanceSubjectPoint] is an inspectable local semantic convergence around a declared focus
  + [resonance_uuid] is the stable primary identity
  + [focus_term_anchor_set] is the declared attention-window focus
  + [subject_scope_uuid] is the local subject boundary
  + [semantic_axis] is the declared dimension along which meanings correlate
  + [association_declaration_set] is explicit SOP or Attention relations holding the pattern together
  + [coherence_score] is an explainable aggregation of compatible correlation weights
  + [precision_score] is the degree to which the pattern excludes competing meanings
  + [supporting_capability_set] is SOP forms, features, and functions addressed by the resonance
  + [source_file_set] is the authoritative files carrying the declarations
  + [formation_turn_uuid] is the intention-bearing turn that formed or revised the point
  + [status] is candidate, resonating, ambiguous, contradicted, stale, or retired
  = must: remain inspectable as declarations, weights, files, and lineage
  = must: record negative and contradictory associations as well as reinforcing ones
  - never: equate activation strength inside a model with proven semantic coherence

& [AttentionResonanceProjection] is the reproducible prompt projection of a ResonanceSubjectPoint into a model context
  + [projection_uuid] is the stable primary identity
  + [resonance_uuid] is the database subject being projected
  + [declared_focus_terms] is the ordered focus-anchor block
  + [association_declarations] is the ordered SOP or Attention relation block
  + [purpose_directive] is the intended inference operation
  + [source_digest_set] is the content identity of projected authority
  + [prompt_template_version] is the projection contract
  + [model_context_parameters] is model identity, context size, retained-prefix policy, and cache identity
  + [projection_result] is structured inference output and citations
  = must: distinguish durable database association from transient model attention
  = must: fit within an explicit token budget with priority and omission records
  = must: be reproducible from the same records, template, and model parameters

& [PurposeAttentionBinding] is the durable binding between an intended purpose and the semantic material selected for attention
  + [binding_uuid] is the stable primary identity
  + [purpose_anchor_uuid] is the intended outcome or question
  + [focus_subject_uuid] is the local identity currently under inspection
  + [resonance_uuid_set] is the coherent subject points admitted into attention
  + [relation_policy] is the edge kinds, directions, weights, and exclusions permitted during navigation
  + [reentry_condition] is the coherence, evidence, or workflow state that activates the binding again
  + [projection_priority] is the ordering used under finite context capacity
  + [binding_digest] is the deterministic identity of the binding contents and policy
  + [lifecycle_state] is proposed, active, dormant, reentered, superseded, or retired
  = must: be stored outside model context and projected into inference when needed
  = must: preserve why each association was admitted or excluded

& [SemanticNavigationLens] is a purpose-conditioned instrument for focusing identity and meaning
  + [lens_uuid] is the stable lens configuration identity
  + [purpose_binding_uuid] is the governing PurposeAttentionBinding
  + [focal_subject_uuid] is the center of the current view
  + [semantic_axis_set] is the dimensions relevant to the purpose
  + [distance_policy] is WeightedSemanticDistance
  + [viewport] is a bounded BallGraphViewport
  + [traversal_trace] is the inspectable path by which attention reached the focal subject
  + [peek_policy] is the bounded rule for looking through or around intersecting subjects
  = must: change the visible neighborhood when purpose changes without changing stored source meaning
  - never: treat the viewport as the complete semantic forest

& [WeightedSemanticDistance] is purpose-relative separation across typed associations
  + [hop_count] is the number of traversed direct relations
  + [edge_weight_sum] is the accumulated correlation cost or affinity
  + [edge_type_cost] is the cost assigned to each relation kind
  + [direction_penalty] is the cost of traversing against directed meaning
  + [subject_boundary_cost] is the cost of crossing contextual scope
  + [authority_penalty] is the cost of weak, stale, disputed, or noncanonical support
  + [purpose_alignment_gain] is the reduction for relations that directly support the active intention
  + [contradiction_penalty] is the cost of incompatible meaning
  + [uncertainty] is the confidence interval or unresolved distance component
  = must: report hop count separately from weighted distance
  = must: allow two equal-hop paths to have different semantic distances

& [BallGraphViewport] is the bounded neighborhood presented around one focal subject
  + [viewport_uuid] is the stable observation identity
  + [center_subject_uuid] is the current focal point
  + [radius_budget] is maximum hops, weighted cost, node count, token cost, or a combination
  + [visible_node_set] is subjects admitted by the lens policy
  + [visible_edge_set] is typed relations among visible subjects
  + [pants_junction_set] is composition and decomposition transitions visible in the neighborhood
  + [frontier_node_set] is clipped subjects available for a later peek or traversal
  + [omission_record_set] is excluded or clipped material and reasons
  = must: preserve stable subject identities across refocusing
  = must: make the clipped frontier inspectable

& [PantsRelationshipJunction] is a navigable composition or decomposition point
  + [junction_uuid] is the stable primary identity
  + [waist_anchor_uuid] is the composite subject
  + [leg_anchor_set] is the distinguishable component or branch subjects
  + [transform_protocol_anchor_uuid] is the declared composition or decomposition rule
  + [lineage_edge_set] is the shared semantic surface connecting waist and legs
  + [orientation] is compose_toward_waist or decompose_toward_legs
  + [local_curvature] is an optional navigation measure for branching expansion
  = must: allow attention to traverse through the junction in either admissible direction
  - never: use hyperbolic language as proof that the stored graph has literal hyperbolic geometry

& [FacultyTraversalDirective] is one faculty's bounded purpose and judgment contract for semantic navigation
  + [directive_uuid] is the stable primary identity
  + [faculty_anchor_uuid] is the governing faculty identity
  + [faculty_purpose] is the feature of the traversal the faculty accounts for
  + [field_noun] is the focused object the faculty judges
  + [boundary_noun] is the identity distinction the faculty must preserve
  + [residual_noun] is what the faculty leaves unresolved or outside
  + [admissibility_rule_set] is the rules an association jump must satisfy
  + [measurement_obligation_set] is evidence, risks, costs, uncertainty, and purpose progress the faculty must account for
  + [stop_condition_set] is the faults that prohibit or suspend traversal
  + [authority_boundary] is the limit beyond which the faculty cannot decide alone
  = must: judge identity integrity within faculty purpose before considering path distance
  = must: preserve unresolved residuals instead of forcing agreement
  - never: allow a faculty to redefine a subject outside its bounded authority

& [FacultyAssociationJudgment] is the inspectable evaluation of one proposed association jump
  + [judgment_uuid] is the stable primary identity
  + [source_subject_uuid] is the current identity
  + [relation_uuid] is the proposed typed association
  + [target_subject_uuid] is the candidate next identity
  + [active_purpose_binding_uuid] is the intended purpose being served
  + [faculty_directive_uuid] is the governing FacultyTraversalDirective
  + [source_boundary_state] is preserved, qualified, crossed, violated, or uncertain
  + [target_identity_state] is supported, provisional, conflicted, misidentified, or outside
  + [relation_integrity_state] is admissible, qualified, contradicted, unsafe, or unresolved
  + [evidence_account] is sources and support inspected
  + [honesty_account] is claims, assumptions, contradictions, uncertainty, and fair representation
  + [security_account] is integrity, permissions, protected work, stability, and risk
  + [measurement_account] is values observed, method, units or scale, confidence, and omissions
  + [purpose_progress] is supports, neutral, diverts, blocks, or fulfills
  + [disposition] is permit, qualify, reconcile, defer, reject, or stop
  = must: exist before a proposed jump can be ranked by distance

& [FacultyPerspectiveReconciliation] is the balanced preservation and integration of faculty judgments
  + [reconciliation_uuid] is the stable primary identity
  + [judgment_set] is the participating FacultyAssociationJudgment records
  + [agreement_set] is compatible conclusions
  + [difference_set] is distinct perspectives that remain valid
  + [conflict_set] is incompatible claims or directives
  + [honesty_security_gate] is the mandatory truth and safety result
  + [balance_assessment] is whether any faculty dominates beyond its authority
  + [reconciled_boundary] is the identity boundary shared by the admissible perspectives
  + [remaining_residual_set] is uncertainty and unresolved difference
  + [collective_disposition] is permit, qualify, seek_evidence, change_purpose, defer, reject, or stop
  = must: reconcile differences without collapsing meaningful perspective
  = must: stop when truth, safety, subject continuity, or balance fails

& [PurposeFulfillmentChart] is the inspectable route from intended purpose through faculty-governed traversal
  + [chart_uuid] is the stable primary identity
  + [purpose_binding_uuid] is the governing PurposeAttentionBinding
  + [required_condition_set] is what fulfillment means
  + [traversal_step_set] is ordered permitted association jumps
  + [faculty_judgment_set] is judgments supporting each step
  + [measurement_ledger] is all measured values, omissions, evidence, uncertainty, and cost
  + [reconciliation_set] is perspective integration at contested steps
  + [progress_state] is not_started, exploring, supported, blocked, fulfilled, contradicted, or abandoned
  + [fulfillment_evidence_set] is the proof that intended conditions were met
  = must: keep purpose progress inspectable throughout traversal
  - never: equate arriving at a nearby subject with fulfilling the intended purpose

~ [Dimension255ForestHypothesis] is a provisional representational hypothesis
  + [candidate_meaning] is up to 255 declared semantic axes, channels, roles, or address dimensions may form a compact navigation vocabulary
  + [current_status] is metaphor_and_design_pressure_not_validated_geometry
  = must: validate whether 255 is an intrinsic invariant, carrier limit, or useful encoding choice before formation

& [SOPCapabilityRecord] is an indexed declaration of an accessible form, feature, or function
  + [capability_uuid] is the stable primary identity
  + [capability_kind] is form, feature, function, workflow, constraint, or interface
  + [declaring_subject_anchor_uuid] is the SOP subject that owns the capability
  + [file_reference_uuid] is the authoritative declaring file
  + [locator] is the bounded declaration location
  + [input_contract_anchor_set] is required semantic inputs
  + [output_contract_anchor_set] is declared semantic outputs
  + [guard_set] is conditions, constraints, permissions, and failure boundaries
  + [availability_state] is discoverable, callable, unavailable, stale, or superseded
  - never: equate discoverable with executable

& [SOPIndexRecord] is a discoverability record for SOP content
  + [sop_index_uuid] is the stable primary identity
  + [file_reference_uuid] is the indexed file
  + [subject_anchor_uuid] is an indexed SOP subject or local semantic anchor
  + [locator] is a durable line, block, parser node, or content-address reference
  + [content_digest] is the indexed file or bounded block digest
  + [indexed_at] is the indexing time
  + [indexer_version] is the transform version
  + [staleness_state] is current, stale, missing, or conflicted
  = must: preserve a reference back to the authoritative file
  = must: become stale when the referenced content digest changes

& [FileReference] is an inspectable association to repository content
  + [file_reference_uuid] is the stable primary identity
  + [repository_relative_path] is the canonical project-relative locator
  + [content_digest] is the observed content identity
  + [reference_role] is source, specification, justification, plan, solution, proof, narrative, or implementation
  + [existence_state] is present, moved, missing, or superseded
  - never: use an unbounded external path as canonical project identity without an explicit import record

& [TurnArchiveRecord] is the append-only intention and outcome record for one conversation turn
  + [turn_uuid] is the stable primary identity
  + [conversation_uuid] is the durable conversation identity
  + [turn_sequence] is monotonically increasing within the conversation when known
  + [captured_at] is the archival time
  + [actor_role] is user, assistant, tool, agent, or system
  + [source_anchor_set] is references to preserved user input or inspected evidence
  + [intention] is the explicit purpose behind the turn
  + [attention_subject_set] is the semantic subjects active during the turn
  + [operation_set] is composition, decomposition, indexing, specification, planning, implementation, proof, correction, or archival
  + [result] is the durable change or finding
  + [affected_anchor_set] is semantic anchors created, changed, or referenced
  + [affected_file_set] is repository files created, changed, or inspected
  + [unresolved_frontier] is uncertainty or work remaining
  + [supersedes_turn_uuid] is optional correction lineage

  = must: append a record for every project-relevant turn
  = must: archive intention as an explicit field rather than infer it only from transcript text
  = must: preserve corrections as new records linked through supersedes_turn_uuid
  - never: rewrite prior turn history in place
  - never: claim a complete transcript unless the complete transcript was deliberately preserved
  - never: store secrets or hidden chain-of-thought; store concise rationale, evidence, decisions, and intended outcomes

& [LocalSemanticUtility] is the local deterministic control plane around the semantic database and SOP repository
  + [utility_uuid] is the stable installation identity
  + [query_input] is terms, contextual anchors, intended purpose, constraints, and repository scope
  + [database_interface] is bounded read and policy-controlled write operations
  + [repository_interface] is bounded file discovery, content verification, and authorized mutation
  + [retrieval_output] is ranked SOPCapabilityRecord and FileReference candidates with score explanations
  + [job_interface] is creation, validation, dispatch, observation, cancellation, and archival of bounded jobs
  = must: operate locally by default
  = must: retrieve authoritative files before asking a processor to act on their meaning
  = must: return component correlation weights, provenance, authority state, and staleness state with every ranked candidate
  = must: retain deterministic orchestration paths that do not require an LLM
  - never: hide ranking provenance behind a single opaque score

& [SecretaryProcessor] is an optional replaceable local LLM role specialized for SOP input and output coordination
  + [processor_uuid] is the installed processor identity
  + [role] is secretary_of_SOP_IO
  + [input] is a bounded InferenceJobPacket plus retrieved authoritative SOP capability context
  + [output] is a structured proposal, tool-call request, job result, uncertainty, or refusal
  + [tuning_identity] is model, adapter, prompt contract, tokenizer, and version provenance
  + [authority] is delegated and bounded by the LocalSemanticUtility job policy
  = must: distinguish retrieved authority from generated inference
  = must: cite the SOP capabilities and files used for each proposed action
  = must: emit uncertainty or refusal when capability support is missing
  = may: be absent without disabling deterministic database and repository retrieval
  - never: grant itself new tools, permissions, repository scope, or specification authority

& [InferenceJobPacket] is the durable unit of processor work
  + [job_uuid] is the stable primary identity
  + [requesting_turn_uuid] is the originating intention record
  + [intended_purpose_anchor_uuid] is the semantic purpose governing the job
  + [input_anchor_set] is normalized terms and contextual anchors
  + [resonance_subject_point_set] is inspectable local subject points selected for attention
  + [attention_projection_set] is ordered focus terms and association declarations loaded into model context
  + [retrieved_capability_set] is ranked SOP capabilities selected for the job
  + [allowed_operation_set] is the explicit database, SOP filesystem, Git, or inference operations
  + [repository_scope] is the bounded path and worktree scope
  + [database_scope] is the bounded records and mutation policy
  + [git_scope] is permitted read, diff, stage, commit, branch, or push operations
  + [inference_budget] is model, token, time, retry, and recursion limits
  + [approval_gate_set] is actions that require user or policy authorization
  + [expected_output_contract] is the structured completion shape
  + [job_state] is proposed, validated, queued, running, awaiting_approval, succeeded, failed, cancelled, or archived
  + [result_reference_set] is logs, diffs, database events, commits, outputs, and proof records
  = must: be validated before dispatch
  = must: preserve all state transitions as append-only job events
  = must: make Git and database mutations explicit and reviewable
  - never: infer write authority from read access

^ [ComposeSemanticAnchors] is the SOP pants-composition operation
  + [input_anchor_set] is two or more bounded anchors
  + [composition_context] is the subject and intention governing the composition
  + [output_anchor] is the composite meaning
  + [lineage_edges] is the preserved relation from every input to the output
  = must: keep distinguishable origins inspectable
  = must: emit uncertainty when the inputs do not support a stable composition

^ [DecomposeSemanticAnchor] is the SOP pants-decomposition operation
  + [input_anchor] is one bounded semantic anchor
  + [decomposition_protocol] is the stated basis for separation
  + [output_anchor_set] is the derived semantic legs
  + [remainder] is unresolved or rejected material
  = must: preserve lineage to the input anchor for every output
  - never: invent output meaning absent from source or explicit assumption

^ [IndexSOPRepository] is the transform from repository SOP files to discoverability records
  + [input_scope] is an explicitly bounded repository path set
  + [parsed_subject_set] is SOP subjects and local anchors recognized by the active notation
  + [output] is SOPIndexRecord, FileReference, and relation updates
  = must: be deterministic for equivalent content and indexer version
  = must: report parse faults and stale records
  - never: promote indexed text into canonical authority merely because it is indexed

^ [FindPurposeAddressingFiles] is the weighted correlation and retrieval operation
  + [input] is input terms, contextual anchors, intended purpose, constraints, and repository scope
  + [candidate_set] is current SOPCapabilityRecord and FileReference records
  + [scoring] is inspectable aggregation of applicable CorrelationWeight records
  + [output] is ranked files and capabilities with component scores, provenance, and exclusion reasons
  = must: prefer valid canonical authority when purpose fit is otherwise comparable
  = must: allow negative constraints to exclude semantically similar but inadmissible candidates
  = must: preserve ambiguity when top candidates do not separate reliably

^ [FormResonanceSubjectPoint] is the convergence test for a precise local meaning
  + [input] is focus terms, local subject, semantic axis, association declarations, and purpose
  + [support] is compatible weights, authoritative SOP capabilities, and source files
  + [counter_support] is negative constraints, contradictions, ambiguity, and stale evidence
  + [output] is ResonanceSubjectPoint with coherence, precision, provenance, and status
  = must: require both positive coherence and discriminating precision before status becomes resonating
  = must: preserve the axis and local subject boundary that make the meaning precise

^ [ProjectResonanceIntoAttention] is the construction of a bounded model context
  + [input] is ResonanceSubjectPoint and InferenceJobPacket purpose
  + [output] is AttentionResonanceProjection
  = must: order declared focus terms before their association declarations
  = must: include source locators and explicit uncertainty
  = must: archive which records were omitted when context capacity is insufficient

^ [NavigateSemanticNeighborhood] is purpose-conditioned traversal from a focal subject
  + [input] is PurposeAttentionBinding, focal subject, radius budget, and relation policy
  + [candidate_paths] is typed association paths and pants junction transitions
  + [precondition] is identity boundary inspection and admissible FacultyAssociationJudgment
  + [ranking] is faculty integrity, coherence gain, precision gain, purpose alignment, weighted distance, authority, novelty, and traversal cost
  + [output] is BallGraphViewport, ranked frontier nodes, and traversal trace
  = must: use degrees of separation as one observable coordinate
  = must: rank paths by meaningful relation pattern rather than hop count alone
  = must: exclude distance ranking until identity, honesty, security, and faculty admissibility gates complete

^ [GovernAssociationJump] is the faculty-first judgment sequence for a proposed traversal edge
  + [step_1_identity] is delineate source identity, relation meaning, target identity, inside, boundary, outside, and uncertainty
  + [step_2_faculty] is apply each relevant FacultyTraversalDirective within its authority
  + [step_3_honesty] is verify support, contradiction, assumption, uncertainty, and fair representation
  + [step_4_security] is verify integrity, permissions, stability, protected work, and risk
  + [step_5_accounting] is record measurements, methods, omissions, and purpose progress
  + [step_6_reconciliation] is preserve and reconcile admissible differences of perspective
  + [step_7_purpose] is determine whether the jump advances the charted intended purpose
  + [step_8_distance] is calculate and rank weighted semantic distance only after permit or qualify
  + [output] is FacultyAssociationJudgment and optional FacultyPerspectiveReconciliation
  = must: execute in declared order

^ [PeekSemanticFrontier] is bounded inspection around or through a visible subject
  + [input] is current viewport, selected subject, peek direction, and incremental budget
  + [output] is a child viewport linked to the parent traversal trace
  = must: preserve the former focal point as a reentry anchor
  = must: expose newly crossed subject boundaries and pants junctions

^ [RunSecretaryJob] is the bounded automation operation
  + [input] is a validated InferenceJobPacket
  + [processor] is an optional SecretaryProcessor
  + [control_plane] is LocalSemanticUtility
  + [output] is structured job events and result references
  = must: route every mutation through declared operation and approval gates
  = must: capture repository and database before-and-after evidence
  = must: terminate at budget, cancellation, failure, or completion boundaries
  - never: let recursive inference calls escape the parent job budget

& [FoundationalRequirementSet] is the first traceable requirement collection
  + [FR-001] is preserve terms independently from their contextual meanings
  + [FR-002] is represent contextual anchors and typed relations among anchors
  + [FR-003] is compose anchors while preserving input lineage
  + [FR-004] is decompose anchors while preserving output lineage and uncertainty
  + [FR-005] is index SOP subjects with references to authoritative repository files
  + [FR-006] is detect index staleness through content identity
  + [FR-007] is append one intention-bearing archive record for every project-relevant conversation turn
  + [FR-008] is keep raw dictated sources separate from canonical specification
  + [FR-009] is support correction and supersession without destructive history rewriting
  + [FR-010] is provide traceability from terms and anchors to source, turn, SOP, and file references
  + [FR-011] is provide a local utility that operates the semantic database and bounded SOP repository interfaces
  + [FR-012] is rank files and SOP capabilities by inspectable contextual correlation weights for input terms and intended purpose
  + [FR-013] is index forms, features, functions, workflows, constraints, and interfaces as discoverable SOP capabilities
  + [FR-014] is distinguish capability discovery from permission to execute a capability
  + [FR-015] is support an optional replaceable local LLM acting as secretary of SOP input and output
  + [FR-016] is represent database, filesystem, Git, and inference automation as validated bounded job packets
  + [FR-017] is preserve job state, approvals, evidence, results, and failures as append-only records
  + [FR-018] is keep deterministic retrieval and orchestration usable without the secretary LLM
  + [FR-019] is index an inspectable local ResonanceSubjectPoint where focus terms, a semantic axis, association declarations, correlation weights, and source files converge
  + [FR-020] is project selected resonance records into model context as declared focus terms followed by association declarations and a purpose directive
  + [FR-021] is distinguish durable semantic associations from llama.cpp KV or prompt-cache state
  + [FR-022] is measure resonance using explainable coherence and discriminating precision with contradiction and staleness handling
  + [FR-023] is persist intended purposes and attention bindings independently from transient inference state
  + [FR-024] is provide a SemanticNavigationLens centered on an inspectable focal subject
  + [FR-025] is calculate degrees of separation as hop count while also calculating purpose-relative weighted semantic distance
  + [FR-026] is render a bounded BallGraphViewport with visible subjects, typed edges, pants junctions, clipped frontiers, and omission reasons
  + [FR-027] is support reentry, refocus, and bounded peeking while preserving traversal lineage
  + [FR-028] is treat the 255-dimension forest and hyperbolic-plane geometry as hypotheses requiring validation before literal implementation
  + [FR-029] is define faculty-specific traversal directives with explicit field, boundary, residual, admissibility, measurement, stop, and authority terms
  + [FR-030] is judge source identity, relation integrity, and target identity before semantic distance
  + [FR-031] is require Honesty and Security accounts for every consequential association jump
  + [FR-032] is reconcile faculty perspectives while preserving valid differences and unresolved residuals
  + [FR-033] is record all measured values, evidence, omissions, uncertainty, risk, and purpose progress in an inspectable ledger
  + [FR-034] is chart intended-purpose fulfillment across faculty-governed traversal steps and distinguish proximity from fulfillment
  + [FR-035] is define faculty semantics verbosely before generating condensed attention directives
  + [FR-036] is provide a reversible attention programming language for terminal-style faculty loading and coordination
  + [FR-037] is compile signed Honesty, Security, Scribe, Refiner, Planner, and Weaver contracts into an Observer coordination program
  + [FR-038] is rebuild SOP from inspectable attention state, attention primitives, inference primitives, control operators, effects, functions, and programs
  + [FR-039] is recompile faculty roles as attention-language libraries after primitive semantics stabilize
  + [FR-040] is migrate legacy SOP through typed diagnostics rather than assuming current notation remains canonical
  + [FR-041] is form a provider-independent semantic operating-system layer for attention programs, inference jobs, faculties, effects, persistence, and reentry
  + [FR-042] is withhold operational LLM OS status until scheduling, isolation, effect control, persistence, recovery, and proof execute successfully
  + [FR-043] is support cooperative semantic-boundary negotiation between isolated concurrent model contexts reading identical SOP evidence
  + [FR-044] is identify the attention-first language as SAIL, Semantic Attention and Inference Language
  + [FR-045] is co-form a minimum searchable semantic index after SAIL primitive, state, and intermediate-representation identities stabilize

