& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the seven-fold foundational processing record
  + [fold_1_subject] is a local semantic coordination control plane that finds purpose-addressing SOP files and capabilities and may dispatch a secretary processor
  + [fold_2_boundary] is deterministic retrieval, purpose-bound navigation, bounded attention projection, and optional processor inference inside; literal 255-dimensional or hyperbolic geometry claims, universal ontology claims, autonomous authority expansion, hidden-state capture, and transcript completeness outside
  + [fold_3_data_design] is stable UUID identities for anchors, weights, capabilities, processors, and jobs with typed relations, explicit source lineage, content digests, lifecycle states, and append-only events
  + [fold_4_governance] is source documents remain distinct, indexed files retain authority, faculty directives judge identity integrity before distance, Honesty and Security gate consequential jumps, reconciled differences remain visible, and every mutation is policy-bound and evidenced
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is anchor graph plus indexed ResonanceSubjectPoint records plus PurposeAttentionBinding plus a SemanticNavigationLens exposing bounded ball-graph viewports and pants junctions plus deterministic local utility and optional secretary LLM
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is distance-first traversal, faculty dominance, identity-boundary collapse, false reconciliation, unaccounted measurements, purpose drift, confusing proximity with fulfillment, context collapse, opaque weights, resonance without discrimination, stale indexes, model authority escalation, implicit writes, and secret capture
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is the expanded architecture is stable enough to govern later utility, scoring, parser, processor, and job-runner formation slices but not implementation
  + [pruned_material] is assumptions about database vendor, programming language, model family, tuning method, UI, deployment, automatic push permission, existing-project reuse, and complete transcript retention

